// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`preserves the existing About copy 1`] = `
"About ejuicr
The goal of ejuicr is to a vaper's fist choice for a convenient and easy-to-use ejuice calculator.
Use it Anywhere
If it can load a web page, it can run ejuicr.
We try to keep the UI simple and unobtrusive so that you can use eJuicr easily whether you're reaching past a bunch of bottles for your keyboard or pecking at your phone with one hand and mixing juice with the other.
Install the web app to your desktop or home screen so you can even use ejuicr offline! (coming soon...)
Little to No Setup Time
The faster you can start mixing, the better. So we try to remove as many speed bumps as possible.
If you sign in, you can save your defaults (nicotine strength, PG/VG ratio, etc) to make mixing your ejuice even faster.
No Ads or Trackers - Ever
ejuicr is a labour of love.
We don't want your money or your data.
If there's anything we want from you, it's your feedback.
No Unnecessary Emails - Ever.
We hate spam.
You will never receive emails from us unless you email us for support or request a password reset."
`;

exports[`preserves the existing Contribute copy 1`] = `
"Contribute
Send Feedback
The easiest way to contribute is to send us your feedback by email (feedback@example.test) or twitter (@ejuicr).
We appreciate any feedback you'd like to share.
If you don't really have anything to say about ejuicr right now maybe you could answer one or more of the questions below for us:
How did you find ejuicr?
How long have you been using ejuicr?
When and how do you typically use ejuicr?
Do you find ejuicr easy to use or did you have trouble at first?
What's your favorite or least favorite thing about ejuicr?
Is there a feature you wish that ejuicr had?
Ever had a problem with ejuicr? If so, what was it?
Does ejuicr fail on any devices you've tried?
How likely are you to recommend ejuicr to a friend?
Github
The source code for ejuicr is available on Github.
If you'd like to report a bug or formally suggest a new feature, please create a new issue on the issues page.
Feel free to submit pull request if you'd like to contribute to the codebase. We kindly ask that you clearly document the changes you have made.
Donate
If you'd like to throw a couple bucks our way to help with server costs you can send your donation here."
`;

exports[`preserves the existing Help copy 1`] = `
"Help
Contact Support
If you're having trouble with ejuicr and would like to reach out you can send an email to support@example.test and someone will get back to you.
You can also send a tweet or a direct message on Twitter to @ejuicr but you may have to wait a bit longer for a reply.
Send Feedback
We appreciate any feedback you'd like to share! Please email feedback@example.test or tweet @ejuicr."
`;
